# ============================================================================
# FlowChemistry / Chapman-Jouguet detonation with one-step chemistry  (Hydro2, species.on = 1, chem.on = 1)
#
# The classical non-dimensional detonation: ideal gas gamma = 1.2 (cv 5, R 1), fresh gas rho 1, p 1, T 1 ("Fuel"),
# heat release Q = 50 R T_0, activation temperature T_a = 20 T_0, rate constant chosen so that the half-reaction length
# of the steady (ZND) wave is 1.  Ignited in the MIDDLE of the domain by a slab of hot products (p 60, rho 2,
# |x - 400| < 10): two detonations run outward and the mid-plane is an exact symmetry plane, i.e. a perfect closed end;
# each wave starts overdriven, decays to Chapman-Jouguet and is followed by the Taylor rarefaction that brings the burnt
# gas to rest at the mid-plane.  8000 cells over 800 lengths = 10 cells per half-reaction length (the check uses the
# right-going wave).  Nothing crosses the ends before the waves arrive, so mass is constant and the energy rises by
# exactly Q times the fuel burnt.
# RIEMANN SOLVER: hlle.  With hllc (and its variants, and eventually roe) the strong leading shock, aligned with the
# grid, develops the classical transverse (odd-even / carbuncle) instability on this 4-cell-wide periodic strip: the
# y-variation of the density grows from round-off to O(1) by t ~ 15 and the wave is no longer one-dimensional (also
# without chemistry, with godunov, in one box, with older binaries).  hlle stays one-dimensional to 1e-15; the
# problem has no material interface for hlle to smear.
# (Lessons of the first attempts: a weak driver -- p 45 over 4 lengths -- nearly fails and re-ignites; a zero-gradient
#  end lets burnt gas flow in at u ~ 3.6 and keeps the wave overdriven at +2.4 %; a "wall" made of momentum = 0 with
#  zero-gradient density and energy leaks mass in, +1.8 % over the run.)
# Exact (Chapman-Jouguet, perfect gas, one-step heat release):
#   M_CJ = sqrt(1 + h) + sqrt(h),  h = (gamma^2 - 1) Q/(2 gamma R T_0) = 9.1667   ->  M_CJ = 6.2162,  D_CJ = 6.8095
#   von Neumann spike  p = 42.06, rho = 8.739;   CJ state  p = 21.53, rho = 1.795
#   structure: the ZND ordinary differential equation (integrated in the check script).
# Checks reactive transport end to end: front speed against D_CJ, peak pressure against the von Neumann value
# (resolution limited), the reaction-zone profile against ZND, and the energy / species bookkeeping.
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 8 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowChemistry/input_1D_Detonation plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowChemistry/reference/chemistry_check.py detonation <dir> [<dir> ...]
# ============================================================================
